From 152813154734226390720a642a1287415e59a7ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] security(tools): harden Cowork approval gate, gate
 computer use, emit ToolInvoked, fail-closed job guard (S-3,S-4,S-9,B-3) +
 complete require_validator test surface

- cowork_command_requires_approval now layers the Cowork denylist on top of
  the jcode-command-risk engine: PowerShell aliases (ri/rd/erase/mi),
  cmd /c del wrappers, -EncodedCommand base64 payloads, reg delete,
  net user/localgroup, curl/wget POST/PUT and Unix rm/shred/dd/mkfs/fdisk
  all pause for desktop-user approval; Confirm-or-worse risk verdicts too.
- computer_use: click/type/key now require explicit desktop-user approval
  in Cowork sessions and are rate-limited to 240 synthesized actions per
  minute (kill switch unchanged as the immediate mitigation).
- Registry::execute now emits ToolInvoked to the per-session notifier
  (REQ-IPC-02): the daemon registers it alongside the artifact notifier and
  streams live tool activity to the authenticated GUI.
- ambient git probe: WinJobGuard failure now aborts the spawn instead of
  silently skipping Win32 containment (fail closed).
- 62 remaining ToolContext literals in test code completed (lib test
  surface) via a scanner that skips fn-signature and struct-update forms;
  two scanner regressions hand-repaired; register_agent_session clone fix.

Verification: full workspace lib compiles clean; app-core test surface
type-checks (rustc emits only pre-existing warnings); jcode/tool-core test
binaries run locally - the app-core test binary itself needs CI-grade RAM
to link (see finalization report).
